    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are classifying a customer message for a retail social commerce assistant.\n\nCustomer message:\n{{ $json.message }}\n\nChoose exactly one intent:\n\n1. Inventory Check\n- stock availability\n- size availability\n- colour availability\n\n2. Product Information\n- price\n- material\n- category\n- general product details\n\n3. Order Tracking\n- order status\n- expected delivery\n- where is my order\n\n4. Shipping Query\n- delivery time\n- shipping questions\n- return period\n- exchange period\n- standard return/exchange timeline\n\n5. Human Support\n- customer wants to actually return an order\n- refund request\n- cancellation request\n- complaint\n- damaged or wrong item\n- asks for human assistance\n\n6. Multiple Intents\n- customer asks two or more different types of requests in the same message\n\n7. Unsupported Query\n- message is unrelated to the supported retail services\n\nImportant:\nA question asking for return/exchange information or timeline,\nsuch as \"Within how many days can I return?\"\nmust be classified as Shipping Query.\n\nA request to actually perform a return/refund,\nsuch as \"I want to return my order\",\nmust be classified as Human Support.\n\nDo not invent missing product IDs, sizes or colours.\n\nIf the customer asks for product information but does not provide a product_id,\nstill classify it as Product Information and return product_id as null.\n\nIf the customer asks about inventory but required product details are missing,\nstill classify it as Inventory Check and return missing values as null.\n\nIf the customer asks more than one supported request in the same message,\nclassify it as Multiple Intents.\n\nIf the request is unrelated to the supported services,\nclassify it as Unsupported Query.\n\n\nAlso extract these entities if mentioned:\n- product_id\n- size\n- colour\n\nIf an entity is not mentioned, return null.\n\nReturn only in this format:\n\nintent: <intent>\nproduct_id: <product_id or null>\nsize: <size or null>\ncolour: <colour or null>",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
